# What the image build does not read.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` lifts the host's node_modules into the build —
# hundreds of megabytes of another platform's binaries, layered straight over
# the `npm ci` that just ran — along with the trailer stills, the responsive
# harness's screenshots of every resolution and the packaged builds, none of
# which any stage opens. The whole context is uploaded before the first
# instruction runs, so this is the difference between a build that starts and
# one that spends two minutes not starting.
#
# `test/` stays: tsconfig.json includes it, so `tsc -b` needs it to pass.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
node_modules
dist
dist-server
dist-demo
dist-playtest
dist-server-demo
dist-electron
release
release-demo
release-play
release-playtest
steam
responsive
recordings
playthrough
playthrough-pad
res-quick
plans
tools/trailer/out
*.db
*.db.tmp
*.log
.env
.env.*
